# checks/native-twins.sh --skip file for the legmacs reach list (P6.0).
# <native>  <reason>. Only subsystems that are out of Phase 6 by decision
# (ROUND2.md; they become Phase 7) belong here, never an ordinary twin.
core/eval            in-module eval needs a compiler or interpreter in the module (Phase 7)
core/go*             go blocks need a scheduler on JSPI (Phase 7)
async/go*            same
core/future*         same scheduler (Phase 7)
http/post            vibe's network call; no fetch in the host ABI this round, host-side later (Phase 7)
os/sh                spawning a process has no browser meaning; legmacs' use (shell command) stays native-only
core/defmethod*      reached only through core's print-method multimethod (pr-on, via the tests' printing); the module prints with its own printer and multimethods are the backend's named refusal (defmulti), a subsystem for Phase 7; legmacs defines none
